   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of the\nstate highway system as the \"Sandra L. Wilson memorial highway\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S8555",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8555-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §344-l, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8555\n\nSPONSOR: CARLUCCI\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of\nthe state highway system as the \"Sandra L. Wilson memorial highway\"\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo designate a portion of state route 59 in the Village of Spring Valley\nas the Sandra L. Wilson memorial highway.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 adds a new § 344-1 of the Highway Law designating a portion of\nthe state highway system the \"Sandra L. Wilson memorial highway\".  The\nportion of state route 59 between state route 45 and west central avenue\nin the village of Spring Valley, town of Ramapo, county of Rockland,\nshall be designated and known as the \"Sandra L. Wilson memorial high-\nway\".\n\nSection 2 provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nSandra L. Wilson was a 12-year veteran security guard at the Finkelstein\nMemorial Library in Spring Valley, New York and was dutifully protecting\nlibrary patrons when she was fatally stabbed on February 18, 2020 The\nlibrary is one place multiple communities - Hispanic, Jewish, Haitian -\ncame together to interact and engage. Her shocking passing created a\nsense of unity in the community that the state should honor by passing\nthis legislation.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATION:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediate.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
