    "lawCode": "Add §344-l, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8555a\n\nSPONSOR: CARLUCCI\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of\nthe state highway system as the \"Sandra L. Wilson Memorial Highway\"\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo designate a portion of state route 45, in the Village of Spring\nValley, as the Sandra L. Wilson Memorial Highway.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 adds a new § 344-1 to the Highway Law designating that portion\nof State route 45 in the Village of Spring Valley, Rockland County, as\nthe \"Sandra L. Wilson Memorial Highway\".\n\nSection 2 directs the Department of Transportation to install and main-\ntain adequate signing and provides for the ceremonial nature of the\ndesignation.\n\nSection 3 provides the effective date.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION (IF APPLICABLE):\n\nProvides technical clarifications, and modifications relating to the\ndesignated route.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nSandra L. Wilson was a 12-year veteran security guard at the Finkelstein\nMemorial Library in Spring Valley, New York and was dutifully protecting\nlibrary patrons when she was fatally stabbed on February 18, 2020\n\nThe library is one place multiple communities - Hispanic, Jewish,\nHaitian came together to interact and engage. Her shocking passing\ncreated a sense of unity in the community that the State should honor by\npassing this legislation.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
